Third-party materials
---------------------
sourcedrecall's code is Apache-2.0. Setup downloads the models below, each
under its own terms; the parser and notes models are converted or trained
copies that sourcedrecall publishes on Hugging Face.

- Stanza 1.14.0 (Stanford NLP Group), Apache-2.0. The English tokenizer,
  multi-word token, part-of-speech, lemma and dependency models and their
  character language models and word vectors, converted to ONNX by
  sourcedrecall (sourcedrecall-parser-en). Stanza's English "combined"
  models are trained on Universal Dependencies treebanks (EWT, GUM,
  GUMReddit, PUD, Pronouns) whose licences differ (CC BY-SA 3.0 and 4.0,
  CC BY 4.0, and CC BY-NC-SA for some GUM texts; GUMReddit text is under
  Reddit's terms). Stanford describes the licensing of models built from
  UD data as unclear; see https://stanfordnlp.github.io/stanza/ and
  https://universaldependencies.org. The part-of-speech and dependency
  models use the CoNLL 2017 word vectors (LINDAT, hdl.handle.net/11234/1-1989,
  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), which the archive includes, and character language
  models trained on the One Billion Word Benchmark (no licence stated).
  So the current parser archive is for non-commercial use. A replacement
  trained on UD English-EWT alone (CC BY-SA 4.0) with GloVe vectors
  (Public Domain Dedication and License) and no character language model
  is in preparation (2026-10-13).
- BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5, MIT License.
- cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L6-v2, Apache-2.0; trained on MS MARCO,
  which Microsoft provides for non-commercial research.
- cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-xsmall, Apache-2.0; trained on SNLI
  (CC BY-SA 4.0) and MultiNLI.
- Qwen3-0.6B and Qwen3-1.7B (Alibaba Cloud), Apache-2.0. Modified by
  sourcedrecall: fine-tuned to write notes and quantized to int4 ONNX
  (sourcedrecall-notes-en, optional).
- WordNet 3.0, Copyright 2006 by Princeton University, under the WordNet
  License (https://wordnet.princeton.edu/license-and-commercial-use),
  downloaded by NLTK. Princeton University does not endorse this product.
